# Plumera site rules

## Language split

- **Python** — content builder, APIs (e.g. Corpus), sitemaps, generators, and other non-app tooling.
- **TypeScript / React** — interactive apps only (`npm run dev:app`). Do **not** deliver content pages via the SPA.
- Local Python env: `.venv/` (gitignored). App deps stay on npm.

## Content delivery

- Every content URL is a **full HTML document** (title, description, canonical, body in the file).
- Do **not** use a React SPA / `#root` client router for content pages (local or production).
- Do **not** set title, meta description, or canonical at runtime for content pages.
- **`dist/` is the deployable site.** Local preview serves that same folder as static files; do not add a separate preview rewrite layer.
- Build with the **Python** content builder (`npm run build:site` / `python -m tools.content_builder`).
- Source of truth for copy is Markdown under `content/`.

## Landings vs content pages

- **Landings** (`public/{locale}/index.html`) are hand-authored HTML with a distinct layout.
- The builder **copies** landings and other `public/` assets into `dist/`; it does **not** emit index pages from Markdown.
- `content/core/*/index.md` may exist for editing reference text only; it is **not** a build input.
- All other pages (for now: updates, privacy, votd, …) **must** have Markdown under `content/` and are **emitted** as full HTML.

## SEO / localization

- **No hreflang** alternate link tags claiming translation pairs.
- Canonicals are **self-referencing only** (`https://plumerastudios.com/...` matching that page’s URL).
- Prefer **the same slug/filename** across locales for sanity (e.g. `privacy.html`, `votd/thoughtful-content/`).

## Content layout

```text
content/
  core/{locale}/     # UI locale — updates, privacy (same page set per locale); index.md optional/reference only
  learn/{target}/    # language being learned — votd/, future conjugator/, etc.
```

- `core`: structural equivalence across UI locales (same filenames); body copy is not assumed 1:1.
- `learn`: no required file parity across targets.
- Future UI locales include `ar`, `pt`, etc. under `core/`.

## Build / deploy

- Build: `npm run build:site` or `python -m tools.content_builder` (after `.venv` + `pip install -e .`) → `dist/`.
- Local: serve `dist/` with a plain static server (`npm run preview:site` = `python -m http.server --directory dist`).
- Deploy: upload/sync `dist/` as-is.
- Sitemaps: root index pointing to per-locale sitemaps, generated from files that exist in `dist/`.


## Do not

- **DO NOT MERGE PRs.** Never merge pull requests. No exceptions — not even if the user asks in that conversation. Prepare the PR, test it, report results; the user merges.
- **DO NOT CHANGE CONTENT.** Do not edit user-facing copy (Markdown under `content/`, landing HTML text, chrome/nav/footer strings, template labels, sidebar titles, etc.) unless that exact change is in the current plan or the user explicitly asked for it in this conversation. No drive-by renames, rewrites, or “helpful” wording fixes. No exceptions.
- **DO NOT ADD LARGE FEATURES** outside the agreed plan or discussion. Code fixes and small scoped changes that implement what was asked are fine; new product surface, sidebar blocks, nav items, or other expansions that were not requested are not. When unsure, ask.
- Canonicalize one locale to another.
- Imply 1:1 correspondence between learn content across languages.
- Add SPA meta-patching for SEO on content pages.
- Emit landing `index.html` from Markdown.
- Rewrite content delivery in TypeScript when Python tooling should own it.
